# Analytics & Tracking Rules

> Rules for implementing privacy-compliant analytics and event tracking

## Core Principles

- Privacy-first: GDPR, CCPA, PECR compliant
- Never track PII without explicit consent
- Use server-side tracking when possible
- Respect Do Not Track (DNT) signals
- Document all tracking in privacy policy

## Technology Stack

- **Product Analytics**: Mixpanel, Amplitude, or PostHog
- **Web Analytics**: Plausible (privacy-focused) or Fathom
- **Error Tracking**: Sentry
- **Performance**: Vercel Analytics or DataDog RUM
- **Consent Management**: Cookiebot, OneTrust, or custom

## Privacy Compliance

### GDPR Requirements
- Explicit consent before tracking
- Granular consent categories
- Data retention limits
- Right to erasure support
- Data processing agreements

### Implementation

```typescript
// lib/analytics/consent.ts
type ConsentCategory = 'necessary' | 'analytics' | 'marketing' | 'functional';

interface ConsentState {
  necessary: boolean;    // Always true
  analytics: boolean;    // User choice
  marketing: boolean;    // User choice
  functional: boolean;   // User choice
  timestamp: Date;
}

export function getConsent(): ConsentState {
  const stored = localStorage.getItem('consent');
  return stored ? JSON.parse(stored) : getDefaultConsent();
}

export function setConsent(consent: Omit<ConsentState, 'timestamp'>) {
  const state: ConsentState = { ...consent, timestamp: new Date() };
  localStorage.setItem('consent', JSON.stringify(state));
  
  // Initialize or disable analytics based on consent
  if (state.analytics) {
    initAnalytics();
  } else {
    disableAnalytics();
  }
}
```

